ITEMS = ((('when should i start cpr on an adult', 'what are the signs that an adult needs cpr', 'how do i know when to begin adult cpr', 'when is cpr needed for a grown up', 'what if an adult is not breathing normally', 'how to decide about adult cpr', 'when to begin chest compressions on adults', 'what condition requires cpr in adults', 'how do i recognise a cardiac arrest in an adult', 'when should a bystander start cpr for adults'), 'Start CPR if an adult is unresponsive and not breathing normally, as gasping is not normal breathing. Call emergency services first or send someone to call. Begin chest compressions straight away and continue until qualified help takes over.'), (('how do i check if an adult needs cpr', 'how long should i check breathing before adult cpr', 'should i check a pulse before adult cpr', 'how to shake and shout at an unresponsive adult', 'what to look for before starting cpr on adults', 'how to tell if a grown up is breathing normally during adult cpr', 'should i tilt the head before adult cpr', 'how to check response in an adult collapse', 'what if i am unsure about adult breathing', 'how to assess an adult before cpr'), 'Check whether the adult responds, then look for normal breathing for a short moment. If there is no response and no normal breath, treat it as a cardiac arrest and start CPR. Do not delay to find a pulse unless you are trained, and call emergency services.'), (('how do i do chest compressions on an adult', 'where do i push for adult cpr', 'how deep should adult chest compressions be', 'how fast should i do cpr on a grown up', 'what is the correct hand position for adult cpr', 'should i lock my elbows during adult compressions', 'how to keep compressions going for adults', 'what does good adult cpr feel like', 'can i do cpr alone on an adult', 'how to avoid tiring during adult compressions'), 'Place the heel of one hand in the centre of the chest and the other on top, with arms straight. Push down firmly and evenly, letting the chest rise fully between compressions. Keep going without long pauses and get emergency help as soon as possible.'), (('should i give rescue breaths during adult cpr', 'how do i give rescue breaths to an adult', 'what is the ratio of breaths to compressions in adults', 'can i do cpr without breaths on an adult', 'how to open the airway for adult rescue breaths', 'is mouth to mouth needed for adult cpr', 'what if i am not trained in rescue breaths during adult cpr', 'how long should a rescue breath be for an adult', 'can a barrier device help with adult cpr', 'when to use hands only cpr on adults'), "If you are trained and willing, give rescue breaths after sets of compressions, tilting the head back and pinching the nose. If not, use hands-only CPR with continuous compressions. Call emergency services and follow the operator's advice about breaths."), (('is hands only cpr effective for adults', 'should i skip rescue breaths in adult cpr', 'how to do hands only cpr on a grown up', 'what if i do not want to do mouth to mouth when giving adult cpr', 'can bystanders do adult cpr without training', 'how does compression only cpr help adults', 'when is hands only cpr recommended', 'what to do if breaths are not possible in adults', 'how long to continue compression only cpr', 'should i learn hands only cpr for adults'), 'Hands-only CPR with firm, continuous compressions is better than doing nothing if you cannot or will not give breaths. It helps keep blood moving until an ambulance crew arrives. Call emergency services and keep going until a qualified person takes over.'), (('how long should i continue cpr on an adult', 'when is it ok to stop adult cpr', 'what if the adult starts breathing during cpr', 'should i keep doing cpr until the ambulance arrives', 'how to know if adult cpr is working', 'what if i am too tired to continue cpr', 'when to hand over cpr to another person', 'how long can bystanders do cpr for adults', 'what to do if the adult wakes up', 'who can tell me to stop adult cpr during adult cpr'), 'Keep doing CPR until the person shows signs of life, you are too exhausted to continue, or a qualified person tells you to stop. If the adult starts breathing normally, stop compressions and place them in the recovery position while waiting. Stay with them.'), (('how do two people do cpr on an adult', 'should i swap over during adult cpr', 'what is the best handover for adult compressions', 'can a bystander help with adult cpr', 'how to direct helpers during adult cpr', 'what if two trained people arrive for an adult', 'how often should rescuers change during adult cpr', 'how to coordinate breaths and compressions in adults', 'what to say to someone assisting with adult cpr', 'when to ask a bystander to take over cpr'), 'Two people can share adult CPR, swapping compressions regularly so the rescuers stay effective. Give clear instructions and keep pauses short. Emergency services can guide you over the phone until a qualified team arrives to take over.'), (('is cpr different after adult drowning', 'should i do cpr for an adult after an overdose', 'how to start cpr on a drowning adult', 'does cpr help after electric shock in adults', 'what if an adult collapses after choking and needs cpr', 'is rescue breathing more important after drowning during adult cpr', 'how to warm an adult during cpr', 'what to do before cpr after a near drowning', 'how long to do cpr after a drowning incident', 'when to get help with cpr after drowning'), 'After drowning or an overdose, CPR follows the same priorities of calling for help and starting compressions, with rescue breaths particularly valuable if you are trained. Remove wet clothing and keep the person warm. Tell the operator what happened so they can advise.'), (('what position should an adult be in for cpr', 'should i move an adult before starting cpr', 'how to place an adult flat for compressions', 'is cpr safe if the adult fell from height', 'what if the adult is on a bed when cpr is needed', 'how to protect the airway during adult cpr', 'should i use a cpr pillow for adults', 'what if the ground is soft during adult cpr', 'how to roll an adult for cpr', 'when to avoid moving an adult before cpr'), 'Put the adult on their back on a firm surface if you can do so safely, as soft beds make compressions less effective. If a spinal injury is possible, move them only as much as needed to start CPR. Call emergency services and ask for guidance.'), (('does cpr restart a stopped heart in adults', 'what are the chances of survival with adult cpr', 'should i try cpr if the adult looks pale', 'can cpr harm an adult who is not in arrest', 'what if i am unsure whether to start cpr', 'is it better to attempt cpr than do nothing', 'how quickly must cpr start in adults', 'what to expect after adult cpr', 'who decides when adult cpr is finished', 'when to call emergency services before cpr'), 'CPR cannot always restart a heart, but it can keep oxygen moving to the brain until an ambulance crew arrives with defibrillation and medicines. If you are unsure, call emergency services and start compressions. A qualified team will decide about further treatment.'))
